In Kubernetes, accessModes defines how a PersistentVolume (PV) can be mounted by Pods running on different nodes.

There are 4 access modes available in Kubernetes.
1.ReadWriteOnce (RWO)
2.ReadOnlyMany (ROX)
3.ReadWriteMany (RWX)
4.ReadWriteOncePod (RWOP)

1. ReadWriteOnce (RWO)
accessModes:
  - ReadWriteOnce

Meaning: The volume can be mounted as read-write by pods running on one node at a time


        Kubernetes Cluster
               |
      ---------------------
      |                   |
   Node 1              Node 2
      |                   |
   Pod A                Pod C
      |                   |
      |                   |
      v                   X
  EBS Volume          Cannot mount
      ^
      |
   Pod B

Here:
- Pod A and Pod B are running on Node 1.
- Both may be able to mount the same volume.
- Pod C is running on Node 2 and cannot mount that EBS volume simultaneously.
Important: ReadWriteOnce does not mean only one Pod can access the volume. Multiple Pods on the same node may access it.


2.ReadOnlyMany(ROX)
accessModes:
  - ReadOnlyMany

Meaning: Multiple nodes can mount the volume simultaneously, but only for reading.

           Shared Storage
                 |
          ---------------
          |             |
        Node 1        Node 2
          |             |
        Pod A         Pod B
          |             |
        READ          READ
          |             |
          X             X
        WRITE         WRITE

Both Pods can read data, but neither can write to the volume through these read-only mounts.

3. ReadWriteMany (RWX)
accessModes:
  - ReadWriteMany

Meaning: Multiple nodes can mount the same volume simultaneously with read and write access.

             Shared Storage
                   |
        -----------------------
        |          |          |
      Node 1     Node 2     Node 3
        |          |          |
      Pod A      Pod B      Pod C
        |          |          |
     READ/WRITE READ/WRITE READ/WRITE

All three Pods can read and write to the same storage.

