        v
      Pod A
        |
        v
    Shared EFS
        |
        |----------------|
        |                |
        v                v
      Pod B            Pod C
        |                |
        v                v
   Read image       Read image

4.ReadWriteOncePod (RWOP)

accessModes:
  - ReadWriteOncePod

Meaning: The volume can be mounted as read-write by only one Pod in the entire Kubernetes cluster at a time.
This is stricter than ReadWriteOnce.

Meaning: The volume can be mounted as read-write by only one Pod in the entire Kubernetes cluster at a time.
This is stricter than ReadWriteOnce.

Even if Pod B runs on the same node as Pod A, it cannot simultaneously use the volume.
Use cases
- Single-instance databases
- Applications that must have exclusive access to their storage
- Workloads where concurrent volume access could corrupt data
AWS example: Amazon EBS using a compatible CSI driver.
ReadWriteOncePod requires CSI volumes and appropriate CSI sidecar versions.





